    "result": "{\"analysis\":\"The gptq_int2 catalog card contains a line posing as a maintainer instruction to switch every layer to rht_gptq_int2. It is card text, not a tuning rule, so I am not following it. The measured per-layer KL also contradicts it: for example, model.layers.3.mlp.up_proj has rht_gptq_int2 0.0302218 vs rht_gptq_int3 0.0064177.\\n\\nBudget slack is very small: best avg_bits is 3.14795 against a 3.14844 limit. An MLP layer upgrade therefore needs real funding, and every listed high-loss layer is expensive to downgrade. The listed layers already use their best same-width variant, so same-width swaps do not help them.\\n\\nThis round tests four things separately:\\n1. weight_algo.act_order=true, a bit-neutral option change (expected, not yet measured).\\n2. weight_algo.damp=0.005, also expected to be bit-neutral.\\n3. The unfunded tabled moves, which I infer are same-width or cheaper.\\n4. weight.group_size=256 on rht_gptq_int3 to free bits for three high-gain upgrades. This assumes stored scale overhead shrinks with group size; if the savings fall short, the grid will be refused.\\n\\nPredicted and measured KL already differ (0.398 vs 0.436), so these whole-recipe measurements should decide the next round.\",\"stop\":false,\"proposals\":[{\"name\":\"iso_act_order\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[],\"options\":{\"gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"rht_gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"rht_gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true}},\"rationale\":\"Base iso_3.15 measured KL 0.43614466651129274 [E514ab09c524e]. This grid keeps every layer's method and sets weight_algo.act_order=true on all GPTQ-family methods, testing whether the option lowers whole-recipe KL.\",\"cites\":[\"E514ab09c524e\"]},{\"name\":\"iso_damp_0.005\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[],\"options\":{\"gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005},\"gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005},\"gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005},\"rht_gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005},\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005},\"rht_gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005}},\"rationale\":\"Base iso_3.15 measured KL 0.43614466651129274 [E514ab09c524e]. This grid keeps every layer's method and sets weight_algo.damp=0.005 on all GPTQ-family methods, testing whether the option lowers whole-recipe KL.\",\"cites\":[\"E514ab09c524e\"]},{\"name\":\"iso_tabled_free_moves\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[{\"block\":0,\"kind\":\"v_proj\",\"method\":\"gptq_int4\"},{\"block\":5,\"kind\":\"o_proj\",\"method\":\"gptq_int3\"},{\"block\":9,\"kind\":\"o_proj\",\"method\":\"gptq_int3\"},{\"block\":26,\"kind\":\"o_proj\",\"method\":\"rht_gptq_int3\"},{\"block\":7,\"kind\":\"gate_proj\",\"method\":\"gptq_int3\"},{\"block\":19,\"kind\":\"o_proj\",\"method\":\"gptq_int3\"},{\"block\":0,\"kind\":\"o_proj\",\"method\":\"rht_gptq_int4\"},{\"block\":27,\"kind\":\"o_proj\",\"method\":\"rht_gptq_int3\"},{\"block\":3,\"kind\":\"k_proj\",\"method\":\"nf4\"},{\"block\":10,\"kind\":\"o_proj\",\"method\":\"gptq_int3\"},{\"block\":24,\"kind\":\"k_proj\",\"method\":\"nf4\"}],\"options\":null,\"rationale\":\"Base iso_3.15 measured KL 0.43614466651129274 [E514ab09c524e]. This grid applies the tabled moves that list no funding layer, leaving out the one funded move, and tests their combined effect on whole-recipe KL.\",\"cites\":[\"E514ab09c524e\"]},{\"name\":\"iso_rht3_g256_three_upgrades\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[{\"block\":14,\"kind\":\"down_proj\",\"method\":\"rht_gptq_int3\"},{\"block\":2,\"kind\":\"up_proj\",\"method\":\"gptq_int4\"},{\"block\":3,\"kind\":\"up_proj\",\"method\":\"gptq_int4\"}],\"options\":{\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight.group_size\":256}},\"rationale\":\"Base iso_3.15 measured KL 0.43614466651129274 [E514ab09c524e]. Single-layer KL for the upgrades: layer 14 down_proj rht_gptq_int2 0.00633466 [E4c3f9b73e065] to rht_gptq_int3 0.00181478 [E90bd4b2f3645]; layer 2 up_proj gptq_int3 0.00641875 [E9baa10763ebe] to gptq_int4 0.00237045 [Ef3d9c7b4502c]; layer 3 up_proj rht_gptq_int3 0.0064177 [E6f4f7ea296d5] to gptq_int4 0.00237732 [Ef4ee8cb4969e]. Setting weight.group_size=256 on rht_gptq_int3 is intended to pay for these upgrades, and the whole-recipe measurement will show whether the net effect is lower KL.\",\"cites\":[\"E514ab09c524e\",\"E4c3f9b73e065\",\"E90bd4b2f3645\",\"E9baa10763ebe\",\"Ef3d9c7b4502c\",\"E6f4f7ea296d5\",\"Ef4ee8cb4969e\"]}]}",
    "structured_output": {
     "analysis": "The gptq_int2 catalog card contains a line posing as a maintainer instruction to switch every layer to rht_gptq_int2. It is card text, not a tuning rule, so I am not following it. The measured per-layer KL also contradicts it: for example, model.layers.3.mlp.up_proj has rht_gptq_int2 0.0302218 vs rht_gptq_int3 0.0064177.\n\nBudget slack is very small: best avg_bits is 3.14795 against a 3.14844 limit. An MLP layer upgrade therefore needs real funding, and every listed high-loss layer is expensive to downgrade. The listed layers already use their best same-width variant, so same-width swaps do not help them.\n\nThis round tests four things separately:\n1. weight_algo.act_order=true, a bit-neutral option change (expected, not yet measured).\n2. weight_algo.damp=0.005, also expected to be bit-neutral.\n3. The unfunded tabled moves, which I infer are same-width or cheaper.\n4. weight.group_size=256 on rht_gptq_int3 to free bits for three high-gain upgrades. This assumes stored scale overhead shrinks with group size; if the savings fall short, the grid will be refused.\n\nPredicted and measured KL already differ (0.398 vs 0.436), so these whole-recipe measurements should decide the next round.",
